From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chromium meta-browser maintainers <meta-browser@lists.openembedded.org>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 10:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] named_mojo_ipc_server: use C++ octal literal syntax

Chromium v150 contains a Python-style octal literal in a C++ source file.
Use the C++ syntax accepted by the Yocto Clang toolchain.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [OE-specific]
---
 components/named_mojo_ipc_server/named_mojo_server_endpoint_connector_linux.cc | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/components/named_mojo_ipc_server/named_mojo_server_endpoint_connector_linux.cc b/components/named_mojo_ipc_server/named_mojo_server_endpoint_connector_linux.cc
--- a/components/named_mojo_ipc_server/named_mojo_server_endpoint_connector_linux.cc
+++ b/components/named_mojo_ipc_server/named_mojo_server_endpoint_connector_linux.cc
@@ -121,1 +121,1 @@
-    if (chmod(options_.server_name.c_str(), 0o666) != 0) {
+    if (chmod(options_.server_name.c_str(), 0666) != 0) {
